^warning: ignoring
--
PLR §3.3.2 / §9.4: a non-data descriptor (method) shadowed by an
instance attribute. After `c.m = 99`, reading `c.m` yields 99, not the
bound method. Modeled by giving a method-shadow attr a python_value
storage field + a runtime `__shadow_m` flag: `c.m` reads dispatch via
`if(__shadow_m) instance.m else <nondet>` (the unshadowed fallback is a
sound nondet over-approximation; method CALLS `c.m()` are unaffected and
still resolve via the method-call path). Previously a KNOWNBUG.
